# Opalescence's ruling: "A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack ... only if its controller has
# continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn" (CR 302.6). On turn 3 Bot1 casts
# Opalescence and then Quest for Ancient Secrets: Warleader's Call, under Bot1's control since turn 1, attacks as a 4/4
# (base 3/3, its own +1/+1), while Quest, which came this turn, is a summoning-sick 2/2 (base 1/1 for mana value 1, +1/+1)
# and is refused as an attacker. Quest enters as a creature, so Warleader's Call's "Whenever a creature you control
# enters" triggers (CR 603.6a): Bot2 takes 1 from it and 4 in combat, 20 - 1 - 4 = 15.

